  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is odd function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mo>∵</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>∀</mo><mo> </mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>></mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math> <mo>∴</mo> </math>Graph of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> will be</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/49bbc940-7a45-4925-a495-8090a37655b5-image.png\"/></p><p>From graph, it's one-one and onto both.</p>",
